      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "13.1 Introduction to Cyber Security"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Cyber Security covers the protection of computer systems, networks, and data from digital attacks.",
        "Computer Viruses and Malware represent malicious software designed to compromise or disrupt systems.",
        "Firewalls and Antivirus software form essential defensive mechanisms against unauthorized network traffic and malicious code.",
        "Phishing and Hacking are critical security threats involving social engineering and unauthorized system intrusion.",
        "Cyber Safety Practices are fundamental protocols designed to safeguard personal and organizational digital assets."
      ],
